🧾 What is now Swift-only and why

Swift file Why KMP cannot express it
EngineCustomBlockFactory.swift Conforms to DivCustomBlockFactory and UITableViewDataSource — UIKit protocols with UIView return types. Kotlin/Native cannot implement UIKit data-source protocols ergonomically; the interop is brittle and unsupported.
Info.plist (BGTask IDs) Static build-time resource; no Kotlin equivalent.
AppDelegate registration call 3 lines of glue that call the KMP-exposed registerIosSyncHandler. Everything the handler does is Kotlin.

Everything else — crypto, database, registry, router, sync, state, UI rendering via DivKit KMP, background scheduling logic — is shared Kotlin. The Swift surface is now one factory (~120 lines) and two glue snippets.